  <div class="strip" id="strip" aria-label="Frames from the transition"></div>


  <p class="foot">Black hole: real frames from NASA Goddard's 360° plunge render (SVS 14576, J. Schnittman and B. Powell), camera re-aimed along the same trajectory. In NASA's last frames the top of the sun or the moon is painted in, rising out of the band of light; from there Higgsfield (Seedance 2.5, video extension) continues that footage, eased so its speed matches NASA's at the join, while the line-and-dot print dissolves. At rest a Higgsfield loop holds. The sea rendered in the browser remains as a fallback.</p>
